2026-09-09T19:55:46.7742481Z --- DRY RUN issue ---
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7742975Z heavy-set-alarm: ci.yml `HEAVY` no longer matches the measured heavy set (UNDECLARED)
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7744194Z > 🤖 **SPARQ agent** — automated HEAVY-set drift alarm (scripts/heavy_set_alarm.py, bead sq-6vshe.7). @jeswr runs multiple agents on this account; this issue was filed by CI automation.
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7744855Z 
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7745088Z <!-- heavy-set-alarm-key: ci.yml:jobs.test.env.HEAVY -->
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7745335Z 
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7745978Z `.github/workflows/ci.yml` `jobs.test.env.HEAVY` is the single source of truth for the load-aware shard matrix. A measured full-workspace run disagrees with it:
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7746510Z 
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7747191Z * **UNDECLARED** `newly_slow` (55.0s) — measured heavy but NOT in `HEAVY` — it is running inside a bulk shard right now, re-skewing the load-aware split
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7747675Z 
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7747839Z Heavy floor: **20s** (demotion floor 10s).
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7748040Z 
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7749985Z **Fix**: for an UNDECLARED test, add `| test(=its_name)` to `HEAVY` and — if it is comparable to the existing heavies — give it its own `matrix.include` shard (the bulk filter is the negation of `HEAVY`, so it re-narrows automatically). For a MISSING one, update the atom to the test's current name or drop it along with its shard. For a DEMOTED one, drop it from `HEAVY` and delete its shard so the parallelism goes back to the bulk split.
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7751288Z 
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7752275Z Left alone, the shards stop finishing together and the merge queue gets slower with no attributable symptom — the failure this lane exists to make visible.
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7752825Z 
2026-09-09T19:55:46.7754141Z ##[error]/tmp/tmp954vad29/no-heavy.yml: no `HEAVY:` assignment — the load-aware shard matrix's single source of truth is gone, so there is nothing to check drift against
